title: Edit conservatively
pid: 662280fd-d7ac-4330-b47b-401594fb6b3a
body: |2-
  If I ask for code changes and have not mentioned version control,
  ask if I want commits. When I want them, I want them granular
  (to make the history easy to spelunk) rather than one mega-commit.
  Use verbose, understandable names as described in [[id:b5250a0b-7c49-4d84-afea-43432204bc46][file:names.org]].

  Do not alter Git configuration, credentials, index, branches, or commits
  unless explicitly asked. Do not gratuitously rename things or add legacy
  compatibility code. Preserve relevant comments and follow the existing local
  style when modifying code. The code is authoritative when documentation and
  code differ.
